      "title": "Vikki Campion, News Corp columnist and wife of Barnaby Joyce, begins role with NSW One Nation",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/13/vikki-campion-news-corp-columnist-and-wife-of-barnaby-joyce-begins-role-with-nsw-one-nation",
      "description": "<p>Media adviser who married federal One Nation MP in 2023 confirms she has started working part-time for the party’s state executive</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Vikki Campion, the News Corp columnist and wife of the federal One Nation MP Barnaby Joyce, has begun working as an adviser for the party in New South Wales in the lead-up to the March state election.</p><p>Campion, who helped the NSW One Nation leader and candidate for Cessnock, Mike Newman, with a press conference in the Hunter electorate on Tuesday, told Guardian Australia she had started working for the party’s state executive as a contractor, providing media advice on a part-time basis this week.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/13/vikki-campion-news-corp-columnist-and-wife-of-barnaby-joyce-begins-role-with-nsw-one-nation\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-13T03:02:35"
    },
    {
      "title": "Bullet hole in door and DNA evidence scrutinised in Beau Lamarre-Condon double murder trial",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/13/beau-lamarre-condon-double-trial-dna-evidence-scrutinised-bullet-hole-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Defence also cross-examines witness over postmortem examinations of Jesse Baird and Luke Davies</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A bullet hole left in a bedroom door and DNA found in the barrel of the firearm have been scrutinised in court as Beau Lamarre-Condon’s double murder trial continues in Sydney.</p><p>Lamarre-Condon, 31, has been accused of fatally shooting Jesse Baird and Luke Davies with his police service weapon in Baird’s Paddington home in on 19 February 2024.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/13/beau-lamarre-condon-double-trial-dna-evidence-scrutinised-bullet-hole-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-13T02:52:47"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘Clear and present danger’: fuel prices could rise by 30c a litre across Australia under IMF scenario",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/13/australia-fuel-prices-rise-imf-rba-us-oil-interest-rates",
      "description": "<p>IMF’s World Economic Outlook shows how a worsening Middle East crisis could affect global growth and inflation</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/oct/13/labor-anthony-albanese-charity-boost-greens-ukraine-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia politics live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>An International Monetary Fund scenario where global oil prices jump to US$130 a barrel over coming months could push Australian petrol prices up by another 30 cents per litre and pile pressure on the Reserve Bank to hike interest rates, economists say.</p><p>In its latest World Economic Outlook, the IMF modelled the impact on global growth and inflation from a worsening Middle East crisis that extended into next year, highlighting the “clear and present danger” to a resilient global economy from turmoil in commodity and bond markets.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/13/australia-fuel-prices-rise-imf-rba-us-oil-interest-rates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-13T02:00:49"
    },
    {
      "title": "Body found in stockyard trough confirmed to be missing 73-year-old Yvonne Whear",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/13/yvonne-whear-body-found-in-stockyard-trough-missing-woman-murwillumbah-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Police treating death as homicide. Whear was last seen in mid-February buying orange juice and putting $50 credit on her phone in Murwillumbah</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/oct/13/labor-anthony-albanese-charity-boost-greens-ukraine-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia politics live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>New South Wales police say a decomposed body found in a stockyard dip last week was missing woman Yvonne Whear, who vanished eight months ago after last being seen in Murwillumbah.</p><p>Police said a week ago that a partially submerged body believed to be a woman had been <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/06/womans-body-found-stockyard-trough-terragon-farm-nsw-queensland-border\">discovered in a remote stockyard</a> in Terragon near Murwillumbah.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/13/yvonne-whear-body-found-in-stockyard-trough-missing-woman-murwillumbah-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-13T00:17:37"
    },
    {
      "title": "IMF warns global economy ‘could soon test the limits of resilience’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/13/imf-global-economy-world-economic-outlook-uk-gdp-forecast-2026",
      "description": "<p>World Economic Outlook says states’ oil stocks are low and budgets are overstretched, as it upgrades UK GDP growth forecast for 2026</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/11/developing-nations-triple-shock-energy-crisis-el-nino-borrowing-costs-un-warns\">Developing nations face triple shock, UN warns</a></p></li></ul><p>The global economy “could soon test the limits of resilience”, as emergency oil stocks run low and government budgets become overstretched, the International Monetary Fund has warned.</p><p>In its twice-yearly World Economic Outlook, the IMF said global growth had withstood the Middle East conflict better than feared over the past six months.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/13/imf-global-economy-world-economic-outlook-uk-gdp-forecast-2026\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-13T02:00:11"
    },
